Third-Party Notices
====================

This project targets hardware and reuses driver code originally published by
the Linnes Lab (Weldon School of Biomedical Engineering, Purdue University)
as part of the HELPStat project:

  Bautista, K. A.; Madsen, E.; Riegle, S. D.; Linnes, J. C.
  "HELPStat: A Handheld, EIS-Enabled, Low-Cost, and Portable Potentiostat."
  ACS Electrochemistry, 2025. DOI: 10.1021/acselectrochem.4c00052
  Repository: https://github.com/LinnesLab/HELPStat
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2024 Linnes Lab)

When the ElectroStat firmware is added to this repository, the following
files are adapted from HELPStat's AD5941 driver and firmware and must keep
their original HELPStat/Analog Devices copyright headers unmodified,
alongside this project's own MIT license for the surrounding firmware code:

  - ad5940.c
  - ad5940.h
  - HELPStat.cpp
  - HELPStat.h
  - Impedance.c
  - Impedance.h

No physical or electrical modification was made to the HELPStat hardware
design. ElectroStat reuses the original board and driver as-is, adding WiFi
and USB-serial communication, microSD backup logging, and new
measurement/analysis capabilities on top of it, in the ESP32-S3 firmware,
the Python bridge, and this web application.
